(Results and limitations) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Observed:) Tj
T*
(- Evening visits increased during the four-week pilot.) Tj
T*
(- 30 of 40 surveyed visitors said later closing helped them study.) Tj
T*
T*
(Limitations:) Tj
T*
(- The pilot took place during exam season.) Tj
T*
(- There was no comparison library or control group.) Tj
T*
(- Academic grades were not collected or analysed.) Tj
T*
(- The visitor survey was voluntary and does not represent all students.) Tj
T*
T*
(Interpretation) Tj
T*
(The pilot supports the claim that evening use increased during the trial.) Tj
T*
(It does not establish that longer opening hours caused the increase.) Tj
T*
(It does not establish that extended hours improved academic performance.) Tj
T*
T*
(Recommended wording) Tj
T*
("Evening visits increased during the four-week pilot; the study did not test grade effects.") Tj
T*
T*
(Page 2) Tj
